.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-files-complete - Finalize an upload that hit an ambiguous /files/complete failure


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad files complete [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Replay /files/complete with a saved recovery manifest so an upload that left \fBupload\fR with a complete_state_unknown error can be finalized without re-uploading any bytes.

.PP
The manifest is the \fB\&.error.recovery\fR object from a failed --json upload, or a plain {"upload_id": ..., "key": ..., "completed_parts": [...]} JSON document. Pass \fB-\fR to read from stdin.

.PP
If the manifest includes a file_url, the upload may have already committed on the server; the command will prompt for confirmation (or require --yes) before replaying /files/complete, since a blind re-finalize can duplicate the attachment.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for complete

.PP
\fB--recovery\fP=""
	Path to the recovery manifest JSON (use \fB-\fR for stdin) (required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad files upload ./pack.zip --json > err.json
  jq '.error.recovery' err.json > recovery.json
  gumroad files complete --recovery recovery.json
  # When piping on stdin, --yes is required because the manifest consumes the
  # only input stream and the duplicate-risk prompt has nowhere to read from:
  jq '.error.recovery' err.json | gumroad files complete --recovery - --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad-files(1)\fP
